# Description: GET DATA: read the application transaction counter (ATC) tag.
# Category: utilities
#
# WHAT THIS DOES
# GET DATA reads one single data object from the currently selected
# application, identified by a two-byte tag, without going through the file
# system. The tag used here, 9F 36, is the application transaction counter
# (ATC) kept by payment applications: a counter that increases with every
# transaction. On a payment card you get its 2 bytes back; on cards without
# such an application the same tag simply does not exist and you receive
# SW 6A 88 ("referenced data not found"), which is harmless. This command
# does not modify the card.
#
# THE COMMAND, BYTE BY BYTE
#   80     class byte: GET DATA uses the proprietary/reserved class
#   CA     instruction: GET DATA
#   9F 36  P1-P2: the two-byte tag to read; replace with any tag that is
#          documented for the application you selected
#   00     Le = 0: return the complete object, up to 256 bytes
#
# WHAT YOU SHOULD SEE
#   A small TLV object (tag 9F 36, length 02, then the counter bytes)
#   followed by SW 90 00, or SW 6A 88 if the application has no such tag.
80 CA 9F 36 00
